ies O > M. So O to right of M. Good.\\\\n\\\\nSince L >=5, M either 4 or6. O > M. If M=6 no seat right for O, impossible. Thus M=4 and L=5? Or L=5 M=4; if L=6 M=5 and O>5 => O=6 but M=5, impossible? Wait if L=6, M=5, O >5 means O=6 occupied by L, impossible. So L=5, M=4, O >4. O can be 6? Seat 5 L, seat? O >4 and not L => O=6. Then J < C < L with C and J nonadjacent, C and L nonadjacent. Used positions: M4,L5,O6. Remaining positions 1,2,3 for J,C,H. Need J < C < L (automatic if C in? C<5) and C-J >=2. With positions 1,2,3, C and J nonadjacent => J=1,C=3, H=2. So\\\"},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"length\\\",\\\"logprobs\\\":null}],\\\"model\\\":\\\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\\\",\\\"created\\\":1794483527,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"prompt_tokens\\\":198,\\\"total_tokens\\\":1198,\\\"completion_tokens\\\":1000,\\\"prompt_tokens_details\\\":null,\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":0,\\\"completion_tokens_details\\\":{\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":0}}}\",\"signature\":{\"text\":\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:6029e38f63e1f0440d2d6941ba758c220c2a6b1591f3ab42fe4722c4d087e37b:56f27ae31ec5b9a3a797e05f5ed4b3b49e37587da16d52957c29bd017aedd2d8\",\"signature\":\"0x34d0805d27e3781c3ad601c140b250ace55495f3f6582c2b0de639a9990241b84c7427e3e7081876055a96d2ac048337f46982c07e9f2eb565dc6e9ad43c17261b\",\"signing_address\":\"0x3b753b4406613c5e70ae640508632b600424fa0c\",\"signing_algo\":\"ecdsa\",\"signature_kind\":\"provider_tee\"},\"verdict\":{\"ok\":false,\"reason\":\"no <answer> block\"}},{\"task\":1,\"model\":\"Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8\",\"response\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"2dd90a85bac44bc3ae04159806700691\\\",\\\"object\\\":\\\"chat.completion\\\",\\\"choices\\\":[{\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"To determine the seating order of Cleo, Hugo, Jun, Omar, Liam, and Milo in seats 1 to 6, let's analyze the constraints step by step.\\\\n\\\\n**People:** C (Cleo), H (Hugo), J (Jun), O (Omar), L (Liam), M (Milo).\\\\n**Seats:** 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 (Left to Right).\\\\n\\\\n**Constraints:**\\\