ess next to Fern: |T-F|=1.\\\\n- Fern somewhere left of Omar: F < Om.\\\\n- Olga and Milo not neighboring: |Ol-M| !=1.\\\\n- Dina at one end: D in {1,7}.\\\\n- Olga left of Milo: Ol < M.\\\\n- Tess at one end: T in {1,7}.\\\\n- Quin left of Olga: Q < Ol.\\\\n\\\\nNeed find any permutation satisfying. Let's solve.\\\\n\\\\nT and D both at ends (one each). Since T adjacent F, if T at seat1 then F seat2. If T at seat7 then F seat6. D occupies other end.\\\\n\\\\nCase A: T=1, F=2, D=7.\\\\nThen F<Om => Om seat >2. Q<Ol<M, Ol and M not adjacent. Remaining seats 3,4,5,6 for Q, Ol, M, Om. Need Q<Ol<M< maybe Om anywhere >2. Since Q<Ol<M among 3-6. Need Ol and M not adjacent. With three ordered positions Q,Ol,M in four seats, Ol and M not adjacent. Enumerate seats 3,4,5,6 choose 3 for Q,Ol,M in increasing order; Om remaining. Need Ol-M gap >1. Choices:\\\\n(3,4,5): Ol-M adjacent no\\\\n(3,4,6): adj no\\\\n(3,5,6): Ol-M adj no\\\\n(4,5,6): adj no\\\\nNo? Wait if Q,Ol,M occupy sorted seats, Ol and M are 2nd and 3rd sorted. Need gap >1. Among choose 3 from 4, only skip? (3,5,? M=6 gap1; 3,4,6 gap1; 4,5,6 gap1; 3,4,5 gap1). None. So T=1 impossible? Check Om could be between Q/Ol/M? Constraint Q<Ol<M, Om just >2, but if Om inserted among them, the seats occupied by Q/Ol/M sorted still Q<Ol<M. Need Ol and M not adjacent. With four seats 3-6, three persons Q/Ol/M in increasing order, impossible as above? If Om at 4, Q/Ol/M could be 3,5,6 -> Ol-M adjacent. If Om at5, Q/Ol/M 3,4,6 -> Ol-M adjacent. If Om at3, 4,5,6 adj. If Om at6, 3,4,5 adj. yes impossible.\\\\n\\\\nCase B: T=7, F=6, D=1.\\\\nF<Om => Om >6, only seat7 but T there. Impossible. Wait F=6, Omar must be left? \\\\\\\"Fern sat somewhere to the left of Omar\\\\\\\" means F left of Omar, so Omar >6, no seat. Thus impossible.\\\\n\\\\nHmm both cases impossible? Did I misread? Tess sat at one end, Dina at one end. If T=1, F=2, D=7. Remaining constraints impossible due Q<Ol<M nonadjacent in 4 seats? Let's double-check. Seats 3-6. Need Quin left of Olga left of Milo. Olga and Milo not neighboring. Three persons in four seats with strict order. Is there arrangement Q at3, Olga at5, Milo at? must >5, seat6 adjacent. Q at3, Olga at4, Milo at6 adjacent? 4 and6 not adjacent! Wait I made mistake: sorted positions (3,4,6) Olga=4, Milo=6, gap 2, not adjacent. I erroneously said adj no. Let's enumerate correctly:\\\\n(3,4,5): Ol-M 4&5 adjacent no.\\\\n(3,4,6): gap2 OK.\\\\n(3,5,6): gap1 no.\\\\n(4,5,6): gap1 no.\\\\nSo one pattern: Q=3, Ol=4, M=6, Om=5. Or Q? sorted seats assigned Q/Ol/M in order; if seats 3,4,6, Q=3, Ol=4, M=6, Om=5. Check Ol and Milo not neighboring: seats4 and6 with seat5 between, OK. Omar seat5, Fern seat2 left\\\"},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"length\\\",\\\"logprobs\\\":null}],\\\"model\\\":\\\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\\\",\\\"created\\\":1794483527,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"prompt_tokens\\\":211,\\\"total_tokens\\\":1211,\\\"completion_tokens\\\":1000,\\\"prompt_tokens_details\\\":{\\\"cached_tokens\\\":0},\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":1003,\\\"completion_tokens_details\\\":{\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":1003}}}\",\"signature\":{\"text\":\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:2d882520bb172c8a34ac3c465e3c9b4d447168e87258143319c3c50f83443c1e:7e1e13cdd0511a74ec8648f8a00783b0c0b01d71dcb54974a15301a019b10497\",\"signature\":\"0x6b307f676e7f52f70587038278180b426b42da5997bcae00febf2c3d178895ed6e5f2900c7ef8826e14555d3069910871f249d7c0003f61c6031d96dd3fda9611b\",\"signing_address\":\"0x3b753b4406613c5e70ae640508632b600424fa0c\",\"signing_algo\":\"ecdsa\",\"signature_kind\":\"provider_tee\"},\"verdict\":{\"ok\":false,\"reason\":\"no <answer> block\"}},{\"task\":2,\"model\":\"Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8\",\"response\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"e034775761ea4a02920c892e4b30b8e4\\\",\\\"object\\\":\\\"chat.completion\\\",\\\"choices\\\":[{\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"To determine the seating arrangement, let's analyze the constraints step by step.\\\\n\\\\n**1. Identify the People and Sea